{
  "_note": "LOS MATERIALES — what the world's non-surface families are MADE OF, keyed by the vocabulary that already names them. The surface classes got their own registry on 2026-08-11 (src/assets/surfaces.json); this is the other half of that gate, for the families §13 left open: parcels, greens, piers, street furniture, structures and the minimap.",
  "version": 1,
  "_scope": "MEASURED, not assumed. The audit row said 'duplicated Canvas/Pixi/editor colors'; scanning the tree found canvas ∩ pixi = ZERO — the Pixi backend has no hex literals at all since it started reading surfaces.json — and canvas ∩ editor = 40. Those 40 are what is here, minus the ones that merely SHARE A NUMBER: `#e85d75` is the scooter's paint, a feria cabin and the editor's default feature colour, and `#f3c969` is the tuk-tuk, a ride's trim and a gold coin. Per §13's own rule, an identical number in two files is not automatically one constant, and merging those would only move the hard-coding.",
  "_stays_local": "A shadow alpha, a lamp glow, a bezier ratio or a highlight inside ONE drawing recipe is not a material and stays in that recipe. The test for a row here is whether two runtimes have to agree about it.",
  "parcel": {
    "_note": "Ground fill per ParcelUse — `PARCEL_FILL` in c2d/streets.js and the editor's own parcel palette, which is exactly the pair that drifted before (`market` was live in the manifest and missing from the editor's list).",
    "_key": "churchill/world/enums/features.py :: ParcelUse",
    "plaza": "#7fa87a",
    "_plaza": "UNA PLAZA DE BARRIO NO ES UN ESTADIO. `ParcelUse.PLAZA` existía con CERO usuarios y llevaba el mismo hex que `stadium`, así que Plaza Las Playitas y Plaza Deportes El Carmen se dibujaban idénticas al Estadio Lito Pérez. Un verde más gris y más seco: una plaza es césped pisado y polvo, no una cancha regada.",
    "stadium": "#4f9d5b",
    "garden": "#5ba362",
    "park": "#5ba362",
    "church": "#cfc7b4",
    "cathedral": "#cfc7b4",
    "boulevard": "#d9d6cd",
    "civic": "#c9c2b2",
    "lot": "#b9b2a0",
    "school": "#c8bb96",
    "kinder": "#d3b98f",
    "campus": "#bfb894",
    "market": "#c2b49a",
    "fuel": "#8e9299",
    "_school_note": "A school's ground is its PATIO, not a lawn: the swept concrete-and-earth yard every escuela in the port has, so it reads as a schoolyard beside the green of a park rather than as one more park.",
    "_market_note": "El Mercado: swept concrete, its own manzana. Flat on purpose — it is meant to take a style or an asset of its own later, and this is the plot it will be painted onto.",
    "patio": "#8fae7c",
    "_patio": "EL PATIO DE LA MANZANA — lo que el anillo de casonas deja adentro. Verde, pero no el verde de un parque: es tierra de vecinos con árboles en las esquinas, más apagada que `park` porque no es suelo público y no se entra a ella. Se ve desde arriba por encima de los techos, que es todo lo que hace falta para que una manzana lea como una manzana y no como un bloque macizo."
  },
